# .plan for Bill Zhang (like John Carmack's, but for my GitHub profile)
# What changed on this page, oldest first.

2026-07-23  Rebuilt the profile as a fake operating system. A bot started
            writing the Now section from my public commits twice a week,
            and I added Minesweeper that you play by opening issues.

2026-09-29  Redesigned it as one terminal window on a machine I named
            tianni. Went from fourteen windows down to four.

2026-10-24  Turned it into the gate of 日月神教, the Sun Moon Divine Sect
            from Jin Yong's The Smiling, Proud Wanderer, to match my new
            site, art3m1s.me. I'm a big Jin Yong fan.

2026-10-24  Cut it down to three sections and swapped the moving header
            for a still picture. The old versions are in archive/.

2026-10-24  Put the map from my site at the top. It's the same map you
            get by pressing M on art3m1s.me, and each place on it jumps
            to that part of this page.

2026-10-24  Made Shipped look like the journal in Black Myth: Wukong.
            Each build gets a print of its object from my site's forge
            and one of my real commit messages from that build.
